L000146	\begin{abstract}
L000147	 We performed searches for $\ppX$ where $X$ may be an axion-like particle which promptly decays to two photons, and the first search for $\ppgg$ at the KOTO experiment using data taken in 2021. The search is performed for $X$ mass in the range of 160--220 MeV/$c^2$. Three events were observed in the signal region, with two events near an $X$ mass of 177 MeV/$c^2$. This result led to a range of upper limits on the branching ratio, BR($\ppX$) $< (1\text{--}20) \times 10^{-7}$ at the 95\% confidence level (C.L.). No events were observed for the analysis of $\ppgg$, setting an upper limit on the branching ratio, BR($\ppgg$) $< 1.69 \times 10^{-6}$ at the 95\% C.L.
L000148	
L000149	\end{abstract}
